{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgByLKAL5H8yBz15WHkgz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A React component reads the session through the `useSession()` hook. It is a Suspense hook: it returns a `Session` object or throws a promise, and it never returns `null`. A logged-out user is not an error. The hook returns a `Session` with `authenticated: false`, so components have to check that flag themselves.\n\n**Read path**\n\n1. `useSession()` (`esm-react-utils/src/useSession.ts`) gets the store via `getSessionStore()`. If the store has no loaded session yet, it throws a promise, which the nearest Suspense boundary catches. Once the store loads, the component re-renders, and the hook subscribes to later changes.\n2. `getSessionStore()` (`esm-api/src/current-user.ts`) calls `refreshSessionIfStale()`. That fetches the session when the store is unloaded or older than 60 seconds.\n3. The fetch goes through `refetchCurrentUser()` with `rejectAuthFailure: true`, and `handleSessionResponse()` writes the result into `sessionStore`.\n\n**When nobody is logged in**\n\n- A 401 or 403 from the session endpoint is treated as \"not logged in\", not as a failed lookup. `handleSessionResponse()` stores the `{ authenticated: false, sessionId }` body that the server returned, or calls `clearCurrentUser()` if the body is not a session.\n- `clearCurrentUser()` writes `{ loaded: true, session: { authenticated: false, sessionId: '' } }` into the store. Logout uses it too.\n- In `openmrs-fetch.ts`, a 403 on the session endpoint, or any status in `redirectAuthFailure.errors` when that is enabled, navigates to `redirectAuthFailure.url`. The default is `${openmrsSpaBase}/login`. I did not read the default for `redirectAuthFailure.enabled`, so I can't confirm whether that redirect is on by default. With `rejectAuthFailure: true`, the session fetch still rejects and does not wait for the navigation.\n\n**Caveats**\n\n- I only read `openmrs-esm-core`. I did not check how the app shell or the patient chart uses `authenticated`, so the login redirect behaviour in the running app is inferred from this code.\n- The line ranges below come from the reads. The `clearCurrentUser` range is approximate, since I only saw the start of that function.\n\n**Documentation:** `esm-framework/docs/functions/useSession.md` states the hook's contract (`authenticated == false` when not logged in, never returns `null`). The `getCurrentUser` and `getSessionStore` JSDoc in `current-user.ts` describe the same behaviour.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-react-utils/src/useSession.ts\", \"startLine\": 8, \"endLine\": 116},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts\", \"startLine\": 146, \"endLine\": 167},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts\", \"startLine\": 52, \"endLine\": 74},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts\", \"startLine\": 567, \"endLine\": 602},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts\", \"startLine\": 604, \"endLine\": 606},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts\", \"startLine\": 634, \"endLine\": 636},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts\", \"startLine\": 291, \"endLine\": 300},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts\", \"startLine\": 251, \"endLine\": 277},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts\", \"startLine\": 76, \"endLine\": 142},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/current-user.ts\", \"startLine\": 29, \"endLine\": 32},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/openmrs-fetch.ts\", \"startLine\": 225, \"endLine\": 243},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/